    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1991910049338560566",
      "url": "https://x.com/jason61987/status/1991910049338560566",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/jason61987/status/1991910049338560566",
      "text": "Friday, November 21, 2025, 8:28 AM: Our slow-moving third storm has created significant flooding between the 710 interchange and the five freeway heading southbound this morning. The heavy rain produced up to 2 to 4 inches of rain across many locations in addition to the 4 to 12 inches of rain that fell over the past weekend. \n\nAnother storm system is trending for December 1 through the fifth of 2025 that could bring as much rain or more on top of what we just had. This is due to the consistency of the warming of the Pacific that doesn’t seem to stop heating up across the Philippines to the Hawaiian islands. \n\nAllowing for a parade of storms to slam Southern California, particularly from Santa Barbara to San Diego, but the hardest areas are from Santa Barbara to LA counties even Orange County receives some flooding in Huntington Beach this morning, so no area is unscathed by this atmospheric river and series of storms that continue to strike the region. #CAwx @NWSLosAngeles @realwxforecast @edgarrmcgregor @SoCalweathernet @LaInaMinute",
